      "message": "Thanks Alice, to my knowledge pulling in a prebuilt crate that was compiled with soong and the Android toolchain is not something we\u0027ve done before in trusty and I\u0027m not sure it\u0027s supported since Android and trusty have their own build toolchains. \n\n`FIND_CRATE` is implemented to search over external deps and doesn\u0027t currently search the AOSP tree [1]. Even if it were to be updated, it\u0027s currently just a convenience wrapper and doesn\u0027t bring in prebuilts. Each dep pulled in by `FIND_CRATE` has its own rules.mk file and is built from source using the trusty build system (e.g. [2]).\n\n[1] https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:external/trusty/lk/make/macros.mk;l\u003d19;drc\u003d8c15bc9fc345003fa9d3d8682f581b654c7ddc06\n\n[2] https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:external/rust/android-crates-io/crates/zeroize/rules.mk;drc\u003da992a01e04655e274cf6339b13b2e879bc018594",
